From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:04:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/38] Measure and draw text with Iris's render core

On Linux, OpenSwiftUI links Iris's render core, the Swift package that
OPENSWIFTUI_IRIS_RENDER_PATH points at. The stdout app makes the window's
render core scene with Iris's fonts when it starts, and text is measured by
that scene with the fonts it is drawn with, so frames fit their text.

The default renderer on Linux mirrors each display list into the scene's
layers: colors, rectangles, rounded rectangles and circles in one color,
text, opacity and affine transforms. With IRISRUN_FRAMES=<dir> the stdout
app renders with it, prints each frame as before and also writes it to <dir>
as a PNG. IRISRUN_SCALE sets the pixels per point, and IRISRUN_BENCH=<count>
times drawing each frame that many times into JPEG.
---
